# Nido's ground-floor door: object $3C (Obj_DestroyableDoor, ps2.asm:7961)
# stands in the gap at cell 53,45 with hit-box row 6 in its $2C, so the
# party is stopped on 53,46; A on it is ObjType_Events $18 (loc_DC84):
# $170D, "Maybe dynamite can open this door." Before build 67 npc.c did
# not spawn $3B/$3C and the party walked straight through (this route
# lived in routes/gaps/ with its expect the other way round).

start level 27 53 48         # south of the door, a new game
wait screen level
wait idle
shot 01_south_of_the_door
walk up 2                    # 47, 46
wait step
expect level 27 53 46
press up                     # the door does not give
wait ticks 20
expect level 27 53 46
shot 02_stopped_by_it
press a
wait idle
expect script $170D
shot 03_shut_tight
press c
wait idle
expect level 27 53 46
expect no-stderr not ported
